      <details><summary>Is Pelvic Floor Physiotherapy covered by extended health benefits in Canada?</summary><p>Pelvic Floor Physiotherapy is often claimable under physiotherapy benefits when it is provided by a registered physiotherapist working within their scope of practice. Coverage always depends on your own plan, so confirm with your insurer and the clinic before you book.</p></details>
      <details><summary>How much does Pelvic Floor Physiotherapy cost in Canada?</summary><p>Typical prices in Canada run $110 to $185 per session. Prices vary by clinic, city and what the session includes, and benefits may reimburse part of the cost when the visit is billed under the right category.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Who provides Pelvic Floor Physiotherapy?</summary><p>Pelvic Floor Physiotherapy is provided by a registered physiotherapist. For a visit to be claimable, the practitioner needs to hold the licence or registration their province requires for that profession and bill the visit under the matching benefit category.</p></details>
